- com.rork.acoustical.domain.audio.FocusModeManager
- com.rork.acoustical.domain.audio.WalkieTalkieManager
- com.rork.acoustical.domain.model.AgentAdvice, AgentMode, DistanceMeasurement, DistanceStep, GpsPoint, PanMatrix, PanZone
- com.rork.acoustical.ui.components.DpadDirection — wait, ViewModel is in ui.viewmodel package, DpadDirection is in ui.components. Import com.rork.acoustical.ui.components.DpadDirection. Hmm, that creates a dependency from VM to UI components package — acceptable but better to define direction mapping in the screen and pass axis deltas. Actually cleaner: ViewModel method `moveSpatial(dx: Float, dy: Float)` and the screen maps DpadDirection → dx/dy with sweep step. But sweep factor lives in VM. I'll add VM methods:
  - `fun getSweepFactor(): Float` — private + expose `sweepStepLabel`? The screen needs step label. I'll compute step in VM: `fun moveDirection(dir: DpadDirection)` requires importing the enum. It's fine to import from ui.components (same module). Let me do that for simplicity.

Actually to keep VM UI-agnostic, I'll define in VM:
```kotlin
fun nudgeSpatial(dxStep: Int, dyStep: Int) // -1/0/1
```
and screen calls viewModel.nudgeSpatial(dx = -1...) hmm but the sweep factor multiplies inside VM. The screen maps direction → axis deltas of -1/0/+1 and calls vm.nudgeSpatial(dx, dy). VM applies 0.1f * sweepFactor. Good — no import needed. For the step label, expose `val sweepStepPercent` in UiState? I'll add a computed field in UiState: `val sweepLabel: String get() = ...` Can't easily since UiState is data class with fields isFastSweep/isFineSweep — add computed property in UiState body:
```kotlin
val sweepLabel: String get() = when { isFineSweep -> "Fino ×0.1" ; isFastSweep -> "Rápido ×4"; else -> "Normal" }
```

VM edits list:

A. Imports.

B. UiState fields:
```kotlin
